/000110465926032775/tmb-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b470c06f43c106b245d0f4784ffe58f6df57bfedf4dda700121b5ab8a166c647.bin","sha256":"b470c06f43c106b245d0f4784ffe58f6df57bfedf4dda700121b5ab8a166c647"}},{"id":"f7ad6b5d263ce0a492e615a4721cd65d38dfcb7638dc8f56217bbd8956a37eb2","quote":"b)In December 2012, the Company entered into an agreement to license certain intellectual property relating to the use of all uric acid lowering agents to improve the treatment of metabolic syndrome. Under this patent rights purchase agreement, between the Company and Dr. Richard Johnson and Dr. Takahiko Nakagawa (the “Vendors”), the Company will pay the Vendors a royalty based on the cumulative net revenues from the sale or sublicense of the product covered under the licensed intellectual property until the later of (i) the expiration of the last patent right covering the product; and (ii) the expiration of 10 years from the date of the first commercial sales of a product. As of December 31, 2025, no royalties have been accrued or paid.","context":"The Company will also pay the Licensor royalties on the cumulative net revenues from the sale or sublicense of the product covered under the patent license until the later of (i) the expiration of the last patent right covering the product; and (ii) the expiration of ten years from the date of the first commercial sales of a product. As of December 31, 2025, no royalties have been accrued or paid.","section":"ITEM 19.EXHIBITS","block":1967,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-032775","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001729214","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1729214/000110465926032775/tmb-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b470c06f43c106b245d0f4784ffe58f6df57bfedf4dda700121b5ab8a166c647.bin","sha256":"b470c06f43c106b245d0f4784ffe58f6df57bfedf4dda700121b5ab8a166c647"}},{"id":"